old name inside a string, keyword or symbol that is HASHED, stamped into a descriptor/contract/profile, serialized in a golden or pinned fixture (grep for \"semantic-register\" inside quoted strings/keywords such as :yin.vm.semantic-register/..., contract names, kernel ids, profile digests, error messages that tests pin). Changing such a value changes addresses/hashes. For each such occurrence decide: the rename is the intended identity change (then every pinned hash/golden that moves is REGENERATED in 8f-4, NOT here: list them in the report) or it must stay frozen (then leave it and say so). If the pinned literals in the test suite (descriptor hashes 7b7c6ae9..f3489 and aa757659..7e74c, golden H pairs, A addresses) MOVE because of the rename, STOP and report each one with old/new value and the reason; do not edit literals. Prose \"semantic registers\" meaning the register file stays.\nVerification FOREGROUND sequential: grep proving zero live references to semantic-register / semantic_register in src, test, bb/deps/shadow/cljd configs, scripts (only docs and collab may keep it; list them); kondo `clj -M:kondo --lint src test` no new diagnostics vs a frozen scratch baseline of HEAD; the whole JVM quick tier `clojure -M:test -e :slow` (loopback/antlr may need approval); the ten C4 files' namespaces `-e :slow`; `git diff --check`. No Node/Dart (orchestrator). No commit, no stage. Report ./collab/<ms>-engineer-8f2.report.md with Completed-GMT/Completed-Local/Coding-Agent/Session-ID: moves list, requirer count, danger-class table (occurrence, hashed?, decision), pinned-literal results, counts, truthful. End READY or BLOCKED.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
